{
  "contract": "evidence-job-status",
  "version": 2,
  "owner": "S3",
  "produced_by": [
    "mentat/app/evidence_csv.py:Store.job",
    "mentat/app/evidence_csv.py:Upload.finish (writes import.json state 'reading', then 'ready'/'failed')",
    "mentat/app/server.py:do_GET '/api/evidence-csv?job=<id>'",
    "mentat/app/server.py:Console.collect_evidence (writes collection.json: 'collecting' -> 'completed'/'failed')",
    "mentat/app/server.py:do_GET '/api/evidence-job' (synthesizes 'failed' from a dead pid found still 'collecting')"
  ],
  "consumed_by": [
    "mentat/app/evidence-csv.js: poll ?job=<id> until state != 'reading'",
    "mentat/app/app.js:pollEvidenceJob (collector job)"
  ],
  "description": "Two independent job-status vocabularies that cross the console/collector process boundary and are polled from the client: the evidence-CSV streaming ingest JOB (state reading|ready|failed, catalog non-null iff ready), and the PAC-evidence collector job (collection.json; state collecting|completed|failed, finished_at/message present only once the job is done). Orientation only - the examples are the contract. S3b: the evidence-CSV JOB also carries how the import was read - format, source_kind, source_path, sheet, sheets, encoding, delimiter and header_source - because a file can now be a workbook, a JSON export, an FEC bulk archive or a path on this computer, and the reader is told which of those it turned out to be. The collector JOB is unchanged.",
